  "code": "2265",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1532\" data-end=\"1654\">\n<p data-start=\"1534\" data-end=\"1654\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">This comprehensive AML panel helps in <strong data-start=\"1572\" data-end=\"1626\">diagnosis, prognostication, and treatment planning</strong> for Acute Myeloid Leukemia.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1655\" data-end=\"1761\">\n<p data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1761\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1672\">Karyotyping</strong> identifies chromosomal abnormalities such as translocations, deletions, or duplications.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1762\" data-end=\"2096\">\n<p data-start=\"1764\" data-end=\"1823\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1764\" data-end=\"1779\">PCR markers</strong> detect common molecular alterations in AML:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1826\" data-end=\"2096\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1826\" data-end=\"1912\">\n<p data-start=\"1828\" data-end=\"1912\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1828\" data-end=\"1845\">RUNX1-RUNX1T1</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1850\" data-end=\"1864\">CBFB-MYH11</strong>: Good prognosis (core-binding factor leukemias)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1915\" data-end=\"1974\">\n<p data-start=\"1917\" data-end=\"1974\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1917\" data-end=\"1929\">PML-RARA</strong>: Confirms Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1977\" data-end=\"2029\">\n<p data-start=\"1979\" data-end=\"2029\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1979\" data-end=\"1997\">FLT3 mutations</strong>: Associated with poor prognosis</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"2032\" data-end=\"2096\">\n<p data-start=\"2034\" data-end=\"2096\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"2034\" data-end=\"2052\">NPM1 and CEBPA</strong>: Favorable prognosis if FLT3 is not mutated</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"2098\" data-end=\"2111\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;deal for:</span></strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ul data-start=\"2112\" data-end=\"2242\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"2112\" data-end=\"2146\">\n<p data-start=\"2114\" data-end=\"2146\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Baseline workup of new AML cases</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2190\">\n<p data-start=\"2149\" data-end=\"2190\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Monitoring minimal residual disease (MRD)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"2191\" data-end=\"2242\">\n<p data-start=\"2193\" data-end=\"2242\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Guiding therapy decisions (e.g., FLT3 inhibitors)</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
